{% assign brand_name = settings.demo_brand_name | default: 'Active Paw' %}

<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="footer-shell">
    <section class="footer-brand" aria-label="{{ brand_name }} footer">
      <h2>{{ brand_name }}</h2>
      <p>Pet care essentials for cleaner walks, easier grooming, and everyday routines.</p>
      <div class="footer-trust-row" aria-label="Store confidence">
        <span>{% render 'delivery-promise', format: 'title' %}</span>
        <span>Simple returns</span>
        <span>Secure checkout</span>
        <span>Stock checked daily</span>
      </div>
      {%- comment -%} The only way a visitor abroad can leave the UK market: the store has
          no market web presences. The announcement bar's delivery title links here. {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'country-selector' %}
    </section>

    <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Footer navigation">
      <div>
        <h3>Shop</h3>
        {%- comment -%}
          List the store's real category collections, mirroring the header
          Collections dropdown (every non-empty collection except frontpage).
          Self-maintaining: reflects collections as they are added or retired,
          and stays in sync with the header. Replaced an admin link_list that
          defaulted to Shopify's stock "footer" menu (a lone Search link).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- for collection in collections -%}
          {%- unless collection.handle == 'frontpage' or collection.products_count == 0 -%}
            <a href="{{ collection.url }}">{{ collection.title | escape }}</a>
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Help</h3>
        {%- assign guides_blog = blogs['guides'] -%}
        {%- if guides_blog.url != blank -%}
          <a href="{{ guides_blog.url }}">Pet care guides</a>
        {%- endif -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}#support">Shipping & returns</a>
        <a href="mailto:{{ settings.contact_email }}">Contact support</a>
        {%- comment -%}
          Affiliates entry point is the Shopify page (PRD T10, decision 5c):
          programme copy, an email route and the Apply button to the
          worker's form, which theme.js shows only while the worker answers.
          The page itself needs no worker, so this link never dead-ends.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/affiliates">Affiliates</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}#support">FAQs</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}">Cart</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}?type=product">Search products</a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Routines</h3>
        <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}?q=paw+cleaning&type=product">Muddy walk reset</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}?q=dog+food+water+bottle&type=product">Feeding & travel kit</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}?q=dental+care&type=product">Dental care routine</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}?q=grooming+add-ons&type=product">Grooming add-ons</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <form class="newsletter footer-newsletter" method="post" action="/contact#contact_form" accept-charset="UTF-8">
      <input type="hidden" name="form_type" value="customer">
      <input type="hidden" name="utf8" value="✓">
      <label for="NewsletterEmail">Get bundle ideas and launch offers</label>
      <p>Pet-care picks, restock prompts, and practical offers for easier shopping.</p>
      <div>
        <input id="NewsletterEmail" type="email" name="contact[email]" placeholder="email@example.com" autocomplete="email" required>
        <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-bottom">
    <span>&copy; {{ 'now' | date: '%Y' }} {{ brand_name }}</span>
    {%- comment -%}
      Legal pages, rendered straight from the store's policies rather than a
      menu: menu items that point at policies silently disappear when policies
      are regenerated in admin, so a menu can never be trusted to keep these
      visible. shop.policies only contains policies that exist.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if shop.policies.size > 0 -%}
      <nav class="footer-legal" aria-label="Legal pages">
        {%- for policy in shop.policies -%}
          <a href="{{ policy.url }}">{{ policy.title | escape }}</a>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Hidden until theme.js confirms this browser can actually install or add
      a home-screen shortcut; a dead button would be worse than none.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="button" class="footer-install" data-install-trigger hidden>Add {{ brand_name }} to your Home Screen</button>
    <span>Prices, stock, and shipping are confirmed at checkout.</span>
  </div>
</footer>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Site footer",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
